Q1. Hospital Patient Billing SystemProgram Design & ApproachTo implement the hospital billing system,
we use an Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) approach in Java with a dedicated class to manage
patient data and calculation methods.Data Members: patientId, patientName, roomType, daysAdmitted,
and treatmentCharges.Logic:Room charges are calculated dynamically based on the roomType string 
(General = ₹1,500/day, Special = ₹3,000/day).Total hospital bill = Room charges + Treatment charges.
Java Source CodeJavaimport java.util.Scanner;

class Patient {
    String patientId;
    String patientName;
    String roomType;
    int daysAdmitted;
    double treatmentCharges;

    // 1. Read patient details
    void readDetails() {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter Patient ID: ");
        patientId = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Patient Name: ");
        patientName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Room Type (General/Special): ");
        roomType = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Number of Days Admitted: ");
        daysAdmitted = scanner.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter Treatment Charges: ");
        treatmentCharges = scanner.nextDouble();
    }

    // 2. Calculate room charges based on room type
    double calculateRoomCharges() {
        if (roomType.equalsIgnoreCase("Special")) {
            return daysAdmitted * 3000.0;
        } else {
            return daysAdmitted * 1500.0;
        }
    }

    // 3. Calculate total hospital bill
    double calculateTotalBill() {
        return calculateRoomCharges() + treatmentCharges;
    }

    // 4. Display patient billing details
    void displayBillingDetails() {
        System.out.println("\n--- Hospital Patient Billing Details ---");
        System.out.println("Patient ID       : " + patientId);
        System.out.println("Patient Name     : " + patientName);
        System.out.println("Room Type        : " + roomType);
        System.out.println("Days Admitted    : " + daysAdmitted);
        System.out.println("Room Charges     : ₹" + calculateRoomCharges());
        System.out.println("Treatment Charges: ₹" + treatmentCharges);
        System.out.println("Total Bill Amount: ₹" + calculateTotalBill());
    }
}

public class HospitalBillingSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Patient patient = new Patient();
        patient.readDetails();
        patient.displayBillingDetails();
    }
}


Q2. Airline Ticket Reservation SystemProgram Design & ApproachThis system handles passenger 
reservations, incorporates a bulk-booking discount rule, and computes the final tax breakdown.
Data Members: passengerId, passengerName, flightNumber, ticketFare, and numberOfTickets.
Logic:Total base ticket cost = ticketFare $\times$ numberOfTickets.If numberOfTickets $> 5$,
a 5% discount is deducted from the base cost.GST of 12% is applied to the discounted total amount.
Java Source CodeJavaimport java.util.Scanner;

class AirlineReservation {
    String passengerId;
    String passengerName;
    String flightNumber;
    double ticketFare;
    int numberOfTickets;

    // 1. Read passenger details
    void readPassengerDetails() {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter Passenger ID: ");
        passengerId = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Passenger Name: ");
        passengerName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Flight Number: ");
        flightNumber = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Ticket Fare: ");
        ticketFare = scanner.nextDouble();
        System.out.print("Enter Number of Tickets: ");
        numberOfTickets = scanner.nextInt();
    }

    // 2 & 3. Calculate total ticket cost with bulk discount logic
    double calculateCost() {
        double baseCost = ticketFare * numberOfTickets;
        if (numberOfTickets > 5) {
            baseCost = baseCost - (baseCost * 0.05); // Apply 5% discount
        }
        return baseCost;
    }

    // 4. Display booking and payment details (including 12% GST)
    void displayBookingDetails() {
        double discountedCost = calculateCost();
        double gstAmount = discountedCost * 0.12;
        double finalAmount = discountedCost + gstAmount;

        System.out.println("\n--- Airline Ticket Reservation Details ---");
        System.out.println("Passenger ID    : " + passengerId);
        System.out.println("Passenger Name  : " + passengerName);
        System.out.println("Flight Number   : " + flightNumber);
        System.out.println("Tickets Booked  : " + numberOfTickets);
        System.out.println("Subtotal        : ₹" + discountedCost);
        System.out.println("GST (12%)       : ₹" + gstAmount);
        System.out.println("Final Payable   : ₹" + finalAmount);
    }
}

public class AirlineReservationSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        AirlineReservation reservation = new AirlineReservation();
        reservation.readPassengerDetails();
        reservation.displayBookingDetails();
    }
}
Q3. Vehicle Rental Management SystemProgram Design & ApproachCalculates commercial rental rates based
on category types, complete with optional penalty integrations.Data Members: customerId, customerName,
vehicleType, and rentalDays.Logic:Rental Rates: Car = ₹2,000/day, Bike = ₹500/day.Late return penalty
logic can accept delayed days or flat conditional application.Java Source CodeJavaimport java.util.
Scanner;

class VehicleRental {
    String customerId;
    String customerName;
    String vehicleType;
    int rentalDays;
    int lateDays;

    // 1. Read customer details
    void readCustomerDetails() {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter Customer ID: ");
        customerId = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Customer Name: ");
        customerName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Vehicle Type (Car/Bike): ");
        vehicleType = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Number of Rental Days: ");
        rentalDays = scanner.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter Late Return Days (0 if on time): ");
        lateDays = scanner.nextInt();
    }

    // 2. Calculate rental charges
    double calculateRentalCharges() {
        if (vehicleType.equalsIgnoreCase("Car")) {
            return rentalDays * 2000.0;
        } else {
            return rentalDays * 500.0;
        }
    }

    // 3. Add a late return penalty if applicable (e.g., ₹200/day extra)
    double calculatePenalty() {
        return lateDays * 200.0;
    }

    // 4. Display final rental bill
    void displayFinalBill() {
        double rentalCharges = calculateRentalCharges();
        double penalty = calculatePenalty();
        double totalBill = rentalCharges + penalty;

        System.out.println("\n--- Vehicle Rental Management Bill ---");
        System.out.println("Customer ID    : " + customerId);
        System.out.println("Customer Name  : " + customerName);
        System.out.println("Vehicle Type   : " + vehicleType);
        System.out.println("Rental Days    : " + rentalDays);
        System.out.println("Rental Charges : ₹" + rentalCharges);
        System.out.println("Late Penalty   : ₹" + penalty);
        System.out.println("Final Bill     : ₹" + totalBill);
    }
}

public class VehicleRentalManagementSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        VehicleRental rental = new VehicleRental();
        rental.readCustomerDetails();
        rental.displayFinalBill();
    }
}

Q4. Manufacturing Production Monitoring SystemProgram Design & ApproachTracks and analyzes
factory output benchmarks against performance indicators.Data Members: productId, productName,
targetQuantity, and producedQuantity.Logic:Efficiency Formula: $\text{Efficiency} =
\left(\frac{\text{Produced Quantity}}{\text{Target Quantity}}\right) \times 100$Status:
Marked as Achieved if efficiency $\ge 100\%$, otherwise Not Achieved.
Java Source CodeJavaimport java.util.Scanner;

class ProductionMonitor {
    String productId;
    String productName;
    int targetQuantity;
    int producedQuantity;

    // 1. Read product details
    void readProductDetails() {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter Product ID: ");
        productId = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Product Name: ");
        productName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Target Quantity: ");
        targetQuantity = scanner.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter Produced Quantity: ");
        producedQuantity = scanner.nextInt();
    }

    // 3. Calculate production efficiency percentage
    double calculateEfficiency() {
        if (targetQuantity == 0) return 0.0;
        return ((double) producedQuantity / targetQuantity) * 100.0;
    }

    // 4. Display production status and evaluation
    void displayProductionStatus() {
        double efficiency = calculateEfficiency();
        String status = (producedQuantity >= targetQuantity) ? "Achieved" : "Not Achieved";

        System.out.println("\n--- Manufacturing Production Status ---");
        System.out.println("Product ID        : " + productId);
        System.out.println("Product Name      : " + productName);
        System.out.println("Target Quantity   : " + targetQuantity);
        System.out.println("Produced Quantity : " + producedQuantity);
        System.out.println("Efficiency        : " + String.format("%.2f", efficiency) + "%");
        System.out.println("Production Status : " + status);
    }
}

public class ManufacturingProductionMonitoringSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ProductionMonitor monitor = new ProductionMonitor();
        monitor.readProductDetails();
        monitor.displayProductionStatus();
    }
}
Q5. Online Course Enrollment SystemProgram Design & ApproachManages registration handling, 
academic pricing, and scholarship discounts for digital learning platforms.Data Members: studentId, 
studentName, courseName, and courseFee.Logic:If the base course fee exceeds ₹20,000, 
a 15% scholarship discount is applied.A standard registration fee of ₹500 is added to the
final payable amount.Java Source CodeJavaimport java.util.Scanner;

class CourseEnrollment {
    String studentId;
    String studentName;
    String courseName;
    double courseFee;
    final double REGISTRATION_FEE = 500.0;

    // 1. Read student and course details
    void readEnrollmentDetails() {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter Student ID: ");
        studentId = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Student Name: ");
        studentName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Course Name: ");
        courseName = scanner.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Course Fee: ");
        courseFee = scanner.nextDouble();
    }

    // 2 & 3. Calculate payable amount with conditional scholarship discount
    double calculatePayableAmount() {
        double actualFee = courseFee;
        if (courseFee > 20000.0) {
            actualFee = courseFee - (courseFee * 0.15); // Apply 15% scholarship discount
        }
        return actualFee + REGISTRATION_FEE;
    }

    // 4. Display enrollment and payment details
    void displayEnrollmentDetails() {
        double finalPayable = calculatePayableAmount();
        double discountApplied = (courseFee > 20000.0) ? (courseFee * 0.15) : 0.0;

        System.out.println("\n--- Online Course Enrollment & Payment Details ---");
        System.out.println("Student ID         : " + studentId);
        System.out.println("Student Name       : " + studentName);
        System.out.println("Course Name        : " + courseName);
        System.out.println("Original Fee       : ₹" + courseFee);
        System.out.println("Scholarship Disc.  : ₹" + discountApplied);
        System.out.println("Registration Fee   : ₹" + REGISTRATION_FEE);
        System.out.println("Total Payable Amount: ₹" + finalPayable);
    }
}

public class OnlineCourseEnrollmentSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CourseEnrollment enrollment = new CourseEnrollment();
        enrollment.readEnrollmentDetails();
        enrollment.displayEnrollmentDetails();
    }
}
